{"question": "da da danyi keccel sati didi ko sali do o fuddi larugo iyam sedda sedda ha bandu mako amma balde ji o dilla ni o lari hundeji ko nandi redu be iyam do vurta wakkati fere dada bingel mai do canji den bo dande mako ko o mari vodai den bo o handi dada bingel do o don mara nawugo redu sedda sedda ha less jaburu mako bo kullum to o lari alamaji do berde mako do saka o do tampi ko irin damuwaji do don non fedata bawo dayugo ko damuwa fere don don yande je o yahi asibiti be o do volwa be dadirabe fere se o nani ta be hosa mere kala hundeji be lari fu fe'ata ha bandu mabbe kanjum wadi mo o yidi o lara likita o volwinabe bemde am dume don waddata irin hundeji do bawo dayugo wawan nawugo les redu alama yeu don na alamaji toy dada kesum handi watta hakkilo bawo dayugo mataki toy dada do handi tokka heba yeu do heba mo", "answer": "Iyam e kureeji (clots) vurtooji ɓaawo danygol satti ɗiɗi nandi e heddungo kuuje danygol nder reedu (retained placenta/membranes) malla jonte nder saare danygol, kanjum waddata nawalla les reedu. Tampiri e ɓurtugo ɓernde ma ɗon waddama ngam ustagol iyam (anemia) malla kuuje mettamɓernde ɓaawo danygol.

Kujeji meeraaji ɗi dada kesum haandi lara ngam hakkilango yo: to iyam ɗon vurta ko heewi, urdi mbonndi ɗon vurta, jontere ɓanduu, malla nawalla reedu burtuka. Haandi a yaha asibiti yaasi ngam likita’en ndara ma, ɓe njuurto to woodi kuuje keddiɗe nder reedu ma mbel ɓe njaara ma lobbo.

Kadi, tokkugo yaadu asibiti ɓaawo danygol (postnatal care) e heɓugo siwtaare be nyaamdu lobbu ɗon wallita dada kesum sanne ngam heɓugo sellingo timmungo.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "4", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "1", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "2", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "4"}

{"question": "debbo ɗo danyi ha amin fajira ɗo veyti ɗo danyi de o wari jambi jeytati be fajira mun wondi be mako hasare yoni amin vi debbo ɗo ɓandu mako do diwna bo ɗo wuli sosai den bo o ɗo mari damuwaji ko shafi ɓandu mako je damata mo sosai min yahi min lari debbo mai min suddi mo be kare min auni wolwugo ɓandu mako min tawi 38.2 min wanni mo goɗɗi ɓe nyamu cuufi gam debbo ɗo welnai o nanɗi maleriya min emi mo ko wonɗi ko o nyami o wi wala ko o nyami min yetti mo wonɗi mo wonɗi be mako ɓe hokka mo sha'i o yara min emi mo o musini hande na se o wi de o wari musungo ɓingel may sey o tawi keccel may riwi sey min wi debbo may o umma o joɗa o ɓara ɓawo mako heɓa vallita ɓandu mako hoyna seɗɗa ɗo pat ɗa pat ba amma vallitai bo gite mako laaɓai min sawri mo to nyamini sai o yara paracetamol to o yari paracetamol mai timmi sai min lara dai ɗon hanɗi min hokka mo fahin o ɗo mari malaria kuma min waɗi mo goji mai useni min wawan min hokka mo fahin to o timmini yamugo ɗen bo min sauri mo o yara paracetamol tunda o satai to dillai ni min handi yaudi dim min mokamo min hokka to", "answer": "Based on your description, this appears to be a **postpartum woman (recently delivered) presenting with fever (38.2°C), body aches, and joint pain, with a confirmed malaria diagnosis** — this is a serious situation requiring careful management.

Ndaa ko mi wi'ata:

**Debbo danyɗo ɗo mari malaria e nawnaare ɓalɗe (fever 38.2°C) — ɗum ko caɗtuɗum, kono maa a hokku ɓe uncomplicated malaria** — hokku ɓe **Artemether-Lumefantrine (Coartem)** ko ɓe njarata laabi ɗiɗi ñalnde tati (naange fuɗɗi e hiirnde), tawa ɓe njoni sanne, sabu ɗum ko safaara ɓura moƴƴude e postpartum. Tiiɗno paracetamol e fever jaɓndeeru njarataa mo jaŋgo, ammaa **ndaaru mo no feewi**: to nawnaare heewi (ɗo ɓura ñalɗe tati), to o wuli sanne, to o alaa yarude, walla to o waɗi ndiyam heewɗam (bleeding), yaltin mo yo o yah suudu safrooru mawnundu. Fahin ndaaru **anemia** (ƴiiƴam ustii) sabu o danyi e o mari malaria, so no waawi ndaaru **haemoglobin/PCV** e ndaaru infection goɗɗo (sepsis) sabu 38.2 e postpartum ina foti ndaaru puerperal sepsis. Yamir mo yo o yara ndiyam heewɗam, o ñaama, o dañ boɗɗam, e to fever timmaani ñalnde ɗiɗi, o warta lella.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "4", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "3", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "3"}

